WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.360
Welcome to GitHub Manager We will connect your inventory

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.040
organize it with reviewable intelligence and test the controls

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.380
that keep you in charge

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:16.060
Continue with GitHub opens your OAuth app authorization Complete

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:19.700
that step privately Passwords and authorization screens are

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:20.940
excluded from this recording

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:27.230
After sign in your workspace opens immediately Repository

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:30.590
discovery and organization are separate so useful browsing

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.350
does not wait for an AI run

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:38.090
The header holds GitHub Sync AI organization content settings

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:41.790
and taxonomy browsing The sidebar leaves most of its

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:42.910
space for your structure

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.330
Use Sync GitHub to refresh the accessible inventory The

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:51.470
application reads GitHub data It does not modify your

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:52.070
repositories

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:01.120
My Repos follows ownership collaboration contribution and

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.880
confirmed relationships Favorites follows stars or watches

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.840
with the coverage actually available to this account

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:12.460
Access candidates can include broadly accessible repositories

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:16.920
Open details to inspect the relationship and explicitly include

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:18.700
a relevant candidate in My Repos

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:24.420
Check source coverage after a run Observed partial or

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:27.600
unavailable sources describe what was verified rather than

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.940
promising complete access to every organization

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:35.330
Search names and concepts then refine by language and

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:38.710
visibility Active filter chips make it easy to remove

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:41.350
one restriction or clear them all

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:45.190
The compact cards count repositories in the current scope

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:49.990
Labeled no project needs review and selected answer different

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:51.690
questions with matching icons

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:57.710
Select a repository to see selected subtotals Selection can

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:00.550
span pages Changing the filter clears it with feedback

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:02.770
instead of silently using another cohort

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:08.210
Load more when the inventory spans pages Open repository

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:11.970
details to inspect trusted metadata current memberships and

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:13.430
a durable link back to GitHub

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:18.182
Latest work uses your qualifying contribution dates not a

00:02:18.182 --> 00:02:22.482
repository's last push time Compare the 7 14 30

00:02:22.482 --> 00:02:23.622
and 90 day windows

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:28.620
An empty or partial result is shown honestly The

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.500
contribution observation is bounded and cannot establish

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.340
a complete lifetime activity history

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:39.240
Private repository metadata can remain useful locally Private

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:42.100
readme text and phrases derived from it are excluded

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.860
from the approved model input path

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:47.640
We now use a separate copy of this real

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:51.500
account workspace with the same repositories and saved organization

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.520
Reset and recovery demonstrations leave your working workspace

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:55.960
intact

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:00.400
Open a real public repository from the connected account

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:04.080
Its metadata and extracted evidence support organization

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:08.220
while the original repository remains unchanged on GitHub

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.060
Evidence extraction runs locally It uses repository metadata

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:17.260
and a verified public readme to produce ranked phrases

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:20.200
and source sections with a recorded extractor version

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.640
Open a sample's details to inspect phrases section references

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:29.760
and extractor version The profile supplies short evidence

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.820
that later organization can reuse

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.220
Missing branches remain unknown until verified A missing

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:41.100
readme can use approved public metadata Neither situation

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.140
is a reason to invent repository facts

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:47.830
AI organization lets you choose a taxonomy sample size

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:51.490
and a separate classification batch size Manual selection

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.570
remains available for a precise cohort

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.000
Choose the current filtered view or the entire collection

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:02.340
The preview shows the actual chosen repositories exclusions

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:05.040
processing method and conservative cost bound

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.730
For this walkthrough one small public cohort can produce

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:13.410
a new draft Paid requests remain bounded The rest

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:16.590
of the demonstrations use saved results and local reconciliation

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:22.580
Discover Taxonomy proposes domains projects topics and tags

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:25.480
Start the reviewed run only after checking its scope

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:27.720
Publication is a separate decision

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:32.954
Open review draft to inspect the proposed concepts and

00:04:32.954 --> 00:04:38.114
their supporting samples Edit names definitions aliases or

00:04:38.114 --> 00:04:40.514
a project's parent domain before publication

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:45.530
Save draft preserves your work without changing the active

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:49.990
vocabulary Reopen it to continue reviewing rather than treating

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:52.590
an unfinished proposal as published content

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:57.130
Approve and publish makes one reviewed taxonomy revision

00:04:57.130 --> 00:05:01.030
visible The app validates names and parent relationships

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:03.290
together before committing that revision

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:08.680
Domains group projects Repositories can belong to several

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:12.160
projects Topics and tags are independent facets that can

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.460
cross those project boundaries

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:18.670
Classification compares repository evidence with the published

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:22.370
vocabulary We will use one public repository for a

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:25.710
bounded live check Then inspect the resulting review suggestions

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:30.480
Start the reviewed run and watch its progress and

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:34.240
persisted outcomes Completion describes that bounded cohort

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:36.420
not every repository in the account

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:41.070
Accept a useful suggestion to make it a user

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:44.630
decision A pending suggestion alone does not count as

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:46.070
an accepted repository label

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:50.650
This live result offered an addition which we accepted

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:55.210
Next a local reconciliation example will demonstrate rejecting

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:58.090
one proposal and reviewing several others together

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:03.790
Group suggestions by concept or repository These proposals

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:07.030
come from local matches against the real repository evidence

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:09.430
Reject one when you prefer to keep it out

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:10.290
of your organization

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:14.930
Select only the proposals you intend to decide together

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:19.110
The review summary identifies the exact acceptance or rejection

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:20.870
batch before you confirm it

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:27.050
Confirm the reviewed selection to apply those decisions Stale

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:30.210
inaccessible or conflicting items are checked individually

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:32.550
and reported instead of partially disappearing

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.810
A repository can be labeled by a topic or

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:40.330
tag and still have no project Those coverage counts

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:43.450
must not be mistaken for a failed AI analysis

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:48.530
Successful classification has a durable per repository receipt

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:52.370
independent of detailed run history and the number of

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:53.330
accepted memberships

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:59.390
Preview classification again Already analyzed repositories

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:03.710
reconcile locally by default including valid no match results

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:06.630
The preview shows zero fresh provider calls

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:12.180
Use organization view to distinguish no labels no project

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:16.480
needs review no AI match failed or blocked and

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:17.140
stale analysis

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:22.130
Taxonomy or evidence changes can make an earlier result

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:25.910
stale without clearing its history Extracting evidence is

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:29.270
local preparation not automatic permission for another paid

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:29.590
send

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:35.770
Choose live AI to expose explicit reanalysis This is

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:38.850
a separate choice for meaningful evidence changes expanded

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:41.030
taxonomy or a reviewed retry

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:46.640
Enable reanalyze with AI and give a reason The

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:50.040
resulting preview discloses previously analyzed inputs and

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:51.720
the finite call and dollar bound

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:57.550
Rediscover taxonomy produces another draft Reclassifying

00:07:57.550 --> 00:08:01.450
repositories proposes assignments Neither operation automatically

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:04.130
publishes concepts or accepts model output

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:10.040
We cancel these previews after inspecting them Routine edits

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:13.120
in a missing project do not authorize repeatedly sending

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:14.960
the same repository to a model

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:20.600
Projects keeps the domain to project tree Switch to

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:23.840
topics or tags to browse searchable lists with aliases

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:25.760
and distinct repository counts

00:08:28.010 --> 00:08:31.690
Search a canonical name or an alias Accepted repository

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:35.690
counts and pending review badges remain separate So a

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:37.770
proposal is not mistaken for an existing membership

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:42.820
Browse taxonomy in the header exposes the same modes

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:47.080
Opening the menu loads structure Repository lists are fetched

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:48.520
only after you choose a concept

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:53.300
Selecting a topic or tag opens its matching repositories

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:57.760
Content settings also offers view repositories while retaining

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:59.620
the editing controls for that concept

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:05.210
Drag a repository onto a project topic or tag

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:09.750
to add membership Existing memberships are retained A drop

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:11.310
is not an exclusive move

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:16.460
Dragging a selected row carries the explicitly selected set

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:20.580
Review the repository count and target in the confirmation

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:23.860
dialog before applying a multi repository drop

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:28.080
Drop onto a domain to choose one of its

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:31.780
existing projects Domain coverage derives through projects

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:34.920
The app does not create a direct repository to

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:35.500
domain edge

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:42.020
The open header taxonomy menu also accepts drops These

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:45.480
actions save user assignments locally and do not reset

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.020
prior analysis or call an AI model

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.590
Use the bulk toolbar when a menu is easier

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:56.450
than dragging Select the target concept and add memberships

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.450
to the explicit repository selection

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:03.910
Repository details provides the same manual membership control

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:07.910
for keyboard and touch users Native desktop drag and

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:10.230
drop is never the only way to organize

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:15.660
Remove just one membership and inspect the others Multiple

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:19.700
projects topics and tags are preserved independently with

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:21.640
your user decisions taking precedence

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:27.240
Clear the selection when finished Repository actions use

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:30.300
the current scope selection and the selected card makes

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:32.820
that scope visible before the next operation

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:39.420
Content settings creates domains projects topics and tags

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:43.000
Give each concept a clear name and definition Choose

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.220
a parent domain when creating a project

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:50.270
Rename a project add aliases or change its domain

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:54.850
The canonical identifier stays stable so a spelling improvement

00:10:54.850 --> 00:10:56.630
does not break existing memberships

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:01.190
Try an alias already reserved by another concept of

00:11:01.190 --> 00:11:05.010
the same type The error identifies the exact conflicting

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.710
field and the existing owner

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:13.550
Normalization includes case unicode and punctuation Archived

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:16.870
concepts retain their reservations and an alias repeating

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:19.250
its own canonical name also conflicts

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:23.130
Merge equivalent concepts only after choosing the target

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:26.650
The target retains its identity while memberships and aliases

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:27.770
are reconciled

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:33.410
Separate meanings should remain separate concepts A similar

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:36.250
name is evidence to review not permission for an

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:37.370
automatic semantic merge

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:42.950
Archive a temporary domain and review its dependency explanation

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:46.710
Surviving projects move to the protected unassigned domain

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:51.800
Inspect a surviving project afterward to confirm its parent

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:56.440
and memberships Archived reservations remain visible to validation

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:58.540
rather than being silently reused

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:04.100
In this manually edited saved draft the alias AI

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:07.840
conflicts with an archived domain named AI That explains

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:10.060
why the owning term was absent from the active

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:13.340
tree Another alias points to an active domain

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:18.270
Choose reuse existing only when the meanings are equivalent

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:22.490
The form retains the existing identity and rewrites dependent

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:23.650
draft project parents

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:28.810
Undo last repair restores the previous form You can

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:32.030
instead remove a conflicting alias apply a distinct name

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:35.110
exclude a proposal or edit the field manually

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:41.740
Remove conflicting aliases and save the repaired draft Publication

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.900
still needs explicit approval Checking and repairing the

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:46.380
form uses no model requests

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:51.170
Create a deterministic organization rule using a metadata

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:54.910
field and condition Preview the matching repositories before

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:55.830
approving the rule

00:12:57.700 --> 00:13:00.220
Approve the rule only when it's matches and assigned

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:04.580
concept makes sense Rules apply locally and preserve existing

00:13:04.580 --> 00:13:06.720
user decisions and rejection protection

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:12.460
Run reorganize incremental in rules only mode then inspect

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:16.400
its stored outcomes This is useful organization without provider

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:16.920
requests

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:22.360
Full classification in rules only mode processes the reviewed

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:26.560
cohort through the same local precedence rules Neither control

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:28.640
implies fresh inference for every repository

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:33.060
The budget panel distinguishes window limits from cumulative

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:37.020
money Exhausting a fixed HTTP window does not prevent

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:40.800
manual edits extraction rules or valid cached work

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.460
Manage API allowance can explicitly renew a window with

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:48.680
a reason Here that control affects only an isolated

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.860
test ledger not your real allowance

00:13:52.670 --> 00:13:55.830
Choose selective limit updates to change just HTTP requests

00:13:55.830 --> 00:14:00.430
or just generations Historical usage remains recorded Changing

00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:02.270
a limit does not erase past calls

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:07.650
The original spending ceiling persists through restarts resets

00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:11.890
and new workspaces Unknown remote outcomes retain conservative

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:13.970
reservations until they can be reviewed

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:18.660
Adaptive cost budget bounds are run by dollars and

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:21.920
derives finite call slots It can admit reviewed work

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:24.340
even when a fixed request window is exhausted

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:29.630
Choose a repository count and per run maximum Then

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:33.790
inspect the exact cohort and conservative bound The preview

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:36.130
may admit fewer repositories than you requested

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:42.090
Save taxonomy and classification counts with the budget defaults

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:45.050
Saving preferences starts no work and survives a reload

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:50.060
Already analyzed repositories still reconcile offline in

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:53.820
adaptive mode Selecting a larger dollar maximum does not

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:57.440
bypass privacy analysis protection or the cumulative ceiling

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:02.620
Automatic organization is configurable Weighted changes across

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:05.540
distinct entities can trigger it A configured number of

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:07.980
new projects can also trigger it within the change

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:08.180
window

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:13.940
Choose eligible change types quiet period and cooldown Cosmetic

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:16.700
edits are excluded and a current window explains whether

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:17.720
the threshold is met

00:15:19.380 --> 00:15:22.100
We create two temporary projects and wait for the

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:25.460
real 90 second quiet period The idle middle is

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:28.400
removed in editing The scheduler is not accelerated

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:34.950
The actual scheduler waits for the configured quiet interval

00:15:35.590 --> 00:15:39.310
then reconciles already analyzed repositories locally Any

00:15:39.310 --> 00:15:41.950
idle wait removed from the recording is disclosed

