00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:24.050
and accepted mappings remain unchanged during review

00:18:25.560 --> 00:18:29.240
Reject the draft when the existing vocabulary is preferable

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:33.520
That decision does not delete the published taxonomy or

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:35.300
trigger another classification run

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:40.930
Discovery proposes concepts publication approves vocabulary

00:18:42.150 --> 00:18:45.110
Classification proposes memberships and acceptance makes

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:49.230
your decisions Keeping these steps distinct makes the workflow

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:49.730
predictable

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:55.100
Reset has independent selections for AI organization data

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:59.760
and user taxonomy content Preview the exact dependency counts

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:01.400
before choosing what to remove

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:06.450
The server verifies the impact and limits the preview's

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:10.770
lifetime A changed workspace requires a new preview preventing

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:12.550
confirmation against outdated counts

00:19:14.560 --> 00:19:18.540
The confirmation requires exactly delete Extra spaces do

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:21.640
not pass Change the scope and the old confirmation

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:22.280
is cleared

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:27.060
We cancel this first preview and perform the destructive

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:31.540
checks only in the isolated collection No GitHub repository

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:34.200
or original readiness report is deleted

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:39.430
Before AI only reset retain a manual membership and

00:19:39.430 --> 00:19:43.430
a rejected proposal as witnesses Their protection is independent

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:46.610
from removable AI suggestions and detailed history

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:52.340
Select AI state cleanup inspect the preview type the

00:19:52.340 --> 00:19:56.300
exact confirmation and wait for cleanup verified before continuing

00:19:58.320 --> 00:20:02.780
Core repository data published taxonomy user mappings rejection

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:06.980
protection compact analysis receipts and budget history remain

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:08.200
after verified cleanup

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:13.840
Optional cached restart is still a reviewable proposal and

00:20:13.840 --> 00:20:16.800
honors compatible evidence and prior analysis protection

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:20.740
A missing replay is disclosed instead of starting paid

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:21.180
inference

00:20:22.314 --> 00:20:26.214
Select only domains in the user content checklist and

00:20:26.214 --> 00:20:30.494
inspect the dependency counts Keep AI state cleanup unselected

00:20:30.494 --> 00:20:32.254
to make this a focused test

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:37.480
Confirm the reviewed reset and wait for verified cleanup

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:42.100
Surviving projects are reparented to unassigned rather than

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:43.140
left with missing parents

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:47.940
Browse the projects afterward to check that dependency handling

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:52.600
Repository metadata and independent topic or tag memberships

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:53.460
remain available

00:20:55.740 --> 00:20:59.080
Selective reset is an organizational operation It does not

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:02.200
replenish a budget or remove the historical record that

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:03.540
a repository was analyzed

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:09.010
Now preview all user taxonomy kinds and the intended

00:21:09.010 --> 00:21:13.790
AI state Full reset removes dependent memberships and begins

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.570
a new taxonomy epoch

00:21:17.720 --> 00:21:22.420
Confirm exactly and wait for cleanup verification Repository

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:26.160
inventory and budget history remain Old concept identifiers

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:28.100
are no longer valid assignment targets

00:21:30.310 --> 00:21:32.730
Rebuild the domain and project manually in the copied

00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:36.890
workspace These reviewed concepts receive new identifiers

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:38.930
instead of reviving deleted ones

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:46.000
Analysis receipts still preserve historical processing Another

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:50.080
paid analysis requires the explicit reanalysis choice even

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:52.900
when newly created concepts need more organization

00:21:55.240 --> 00:21:58.340
Expand a persisted run to inspect its method repository

00:21:58.340 --> 00:22:02.580
outcomes failures and any budget result A completed batch

00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:04.720
can still cover only part of the inventory

00:22:06.640 --> 00:22:09.800
No AI match failed or blocked and stale are

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:13.620
different states Existing accepted labels can remain useful

00:22:13.620 --> 00:22:16.300
even when there is no additional model match

00:22:18.160 --> 00:22:21.200
Cached AI never falls back to paid inference When

00:22:21.200 --> 00:22:24.380
a compatible result is unavailable inspect that limitation

00:22:24.380 --> 00:22:26.980
or choose an explicitly reviewed live run

00:22:29.010 --> 00:22:32.290
Read provenance before interpreting a result Fresh live model

00:22:32.290 --> 00:22:36.070
results saved real model evidence and local rules are

00:22:36.070 --> 00:22:38.330
identified separately throughout this walkthrough

00:22:39.440 --> 00:22:42.952
The earlier pretesting and benchmark reports remain available

00:22:43.832 --> 00:22:47.612
They record GitHub access checks named AWS resource tests

00:22:48.552 --> 00:22:51.392
extraction comparisons and real model readiness evidence

00:22:53.240 --> 00:22:56.060
This recording preserves the original walkthrough the voice

00:22:56.060 --> 00:23:00.060
audition and the earlier testing history Its new validation

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:02.220
report maps features to recorded checks

00:23:03.760 --> 00:23:07.500
The working demo uses the approved local application adapter

00:23:08.060 --> 00:23:11.540
Cloud runtime deployment distributed workers and production

00:23:11.540 --> 00:23:13.780
scale operation remain deferred

00:23:15.720 --> 00:23:18.400
Bounded GitHub coverage and small model samples do not

00:23:18.400 --> 00:23:21.640
prove exhaustive access or universal classification quality

00:23:22.580 --> 00:23:25.680
The product keeps evidence provenance and review visible

00:23:27.590 --> 00:23:31.710
For everyday use sync GitHub browse the inventory extract

00:23:31.710 --> 00:23:36.210
reusable evidence review taxonomy and classify only the repositories

00:23:36.210 --> 00:23:37.590
that need new analysis

00:23:39.120 --> 00:23:43.020
Review suggestions then use manual memberships drag and drop

00:23:43.200 --> 00:23:47.220
or local rules to finish organization Missing project coverage

00:23:47.220 --> 00:23:49.620
alone does not require another model call

00:23:51.400 --> 00:23:54.760
Use explicit reanalysis for meaningful changes Configure

00:23:54.760 --> 00:23:58.200
automation deliberately and leave reset until you have reviewed

00:23:58.200 --> 00:23:59.300
its precise impact

00:24:00.850 --> 00:24:05.350
That is the complete local workflow The chapters captions

00:24:06.110 --> 00:24:09.050
transcript and validation report are saved beside the Cedar

00:24:09.050 --> 00:24:10.930
narrated demo for your next rehearsal
